  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The General Services Administration obligated $21.6B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 1,051,858 awards with an average award size of $20.6K, and obligations fell 9.1% year over year. Obligations rose from $17.7B in FY21 to a recent high of $26.5B in FY24, then declined to $23.8B in FY25 and to $21.6B in FY26. The largest spending buckets in FY2026 to date are Computer Systems Design Services at $4.6B and Engineering Services at $3.8B, while the top vendors include BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $1.9B and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $934M. This snapshot reflects partial fiscal-year totals and the mix of professional services, engineering, and manufacturing that dominate current GSA obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the spending trend for the General Services Administration?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration obligated $21.6B in FY2026 to date, down 9.1% year over year. Obligations rose from $17.7B in FY21 to $26.5B in FY24, then fell to $23.8B in FY25 and to $21.6B in FY26. The agency executed 1,051,858 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $20.6K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and vendors capture the most GSA dollars?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services captured $4.6B and Engineering Services captured $3.8B in FY2026 to date. Automobile Manufacturing accounted for $2.3B and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounted for $1.3B. BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC led vendors with $1.9B, followed by SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $934M and HII MISSION TECHNOLOGIES CORP at $847M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does General Services Administration spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration obligated $21.6B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 1,051,858 awards with an average award size of $20.6K, and obligations fell 9.1% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does General Services Administration buy?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration buys Computer Systems Design Services ($4.6B), Engineering Services ($3.8B), Automobile Manufacturing ($2.3B), Commercial and Institutional Building Construction ($1.3B), Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) ($1.3B), and other professional and technical services including All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services ($1.2B)."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are General Services Administration's largest contractors?",
      "a": "BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC is the largest contractor with $1.9B. Other top vendors include SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION ($934M), HII MISSION TECHNOLOGIES CORP ($847M), GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. ($788M), and CACI, INC. - FEDERAL ($774M)."
